BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-202316@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260923T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260923T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260923T183000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Boston\, Our Global Home 
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Waitlis
 t Only\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/202316\n\n5:00P
 M Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion \nWhat makes Boston a truly global city? 
 From the FIFA World Cup and America’s 250th anniversary to the arrival o
 f ships from around the world for Sail Boston\, the city continues to take
  center stage. Yet Boston’s international reach extends far beyond thes
 e marquee moments. Recently named the best U.S. city for foreign multinati
 onals by The Financial Times and Nikkei\, Boston is home to more than 
 50 foreign and honorary consulates\, with one in four residents being bor
 n abroad. Across our universities\, hospitals\, businesses\, cultural ins
 titutions\, and diverse communities\, Boston’s connections span the glob
 e.\n\nFor this ’Quin Chat\, join James Reginald Colimon\, Director of Gl
 obal Affairs for the City of Boston\, and Mary Yntema\, Executive Director
  of the Boston Committee on Foreign Relations and Past President & CEO of 
 WorldBoston\, Inc.\, for a timely conversation exploring how Boston became
  the global hub it is today - and what that means for the people who call 
 it home.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Co
 mplimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask tha
 t all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the ev
 ent.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/202316
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
