SUMMARY:'Quin Chat\; Behind the Curtain - To Kill a Mockingbird
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 100 spots left\n
 Status: Waitlist Only\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/
 203290\n\n6:00PM Reception\, 6:30PM Discussion\nExperience a behind-the-c
 urtain look as The Huntington Theatre Company prepares to present the fir
 st regional production of Aaron Sorkin’s acclaimed adaptation of To Kil
 l a Mockingbird. Artistic Director and Director of the production\, Lorett
 a Greco joins fellow members of the production to explore the art and comp
 lexity of bringing Harper Lee’s enduring classic to the stage\, reveali
 ng what audiences rarely see: the journey from script to stage\, the artis
 tic decisions made along the way\, and the collaboration required to bring
  a production of this scale to life. Together\, they will consider the de
 licate balance between honoring a story that has resonated for generations
  and embracing the creative freedom and fresh perspective that come with a
  new interpretation.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for memb
 ers only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We ki
 ndly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the sta
 rt of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203290
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
