SUMMARY:Sunday Screening: "Pretty Dirty"
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 60 spots left\nS
 tatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/2
 03291\n\n4:45PM Doors Open\, 5:00PM Screening\, 7:15PM Q&A\nGlamorous\, pr
 ovocative\, and unapologetically unflinching\, Marilyn Minter has spent ne
 arly five decades pushing the boundaries of contemporary art. In this Sund
 ay Screening\, filmmaker Amanda Benchley turns the lens on the trailblazi
 ng feminist artist - moving between biography\, studio practice\, and cult
 ural history - to trace Minter’s rise through New York’s art world\,
  the controversies her work sparked within feminist discourse\, and the en
 during influence of her lush\, subversive imagery. Fast-paced\, stylish\,
  and punctuated by notable cameos\, the film offers an intimate portra
 it of an artistwho has continually challenged convention while embracing p
 leasure\, beauty\, and desire as forms of power.\n\nFollowing the screenin
 g\, members are invited to stay for an intimate talkback with visionary fi
 lmmaker Amanda Benchley and Marilyn Minter herself. Together\, they will 
 pull back the curtain on the making of the film\, Minter’s extraordinar
 y career\, and the ideas and experiences that have shaped both her art and
  the film.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. 
 Theatre fare and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cance
 llations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203291
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
