SUMMARY:90 Minutes of Innovation
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 140 spots le
 ft\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/eve
 nts/203300\n\n1:00PM Program\, 2:30PM Networking\nWhat does it take to cha
 llenge convention\, build what doesn’t yet exist\, and turn ambitious id
 eas into meaningful change? In the latest edition of 90 Minutes of Innovat
 ion\, John Werner - venture capitalist\, MIT lecturer\, and Forbes AI colu
 mnist - sits down with Lauren Kuntz\, PhD\, Head of Market Analysis at EN
 GIE\, Gaiascope co-founder\, and founder of the Women’s Greatest Athlete
 .\n\nWith degrees in Physics and Mechanical Engineering from MIT and a PhD
  in Climate Science from Harvard\, Kuntz co-founded the Y Combinator-back
 ed energy forecasting startup Gaiascope\, using AI to advance renewable en
 ergy markets before its 2025 acquisition by ENGIE.\n\nKuntz has brought th
 at same drive to the world of sport. A world-record holder in the 20-even
 t double decathlon and three-time All-American\, she founded World’s Gr
 eatest Athlete in 2024 and the Women’s Decathlon World Championships to
  challenge one of track and field’s longstanding disparities: while me
 n have competed in the Olympic decathalon since 1912\, women never have. N
 ow\, she is helping build the case for the women’s decathlon to finally
  earn its place at the Olympic Games.\n\nTogether\, Werner and Kuntz will 
 explore what it means to pursue ideas before there is a roadmap\, challeng
 e deeply established systems\, and build something entirely new. From ret
 hinking the power grid to reimagining who gets to compete on the world’s
  biggest stage\, expect a wide-ranging conversation about seeing what coul
 d be—and having the nerve to build it. \n\n*This event is complimentary
  and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshmen
 ts will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 2
 4 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203300
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
